---
layout: changelog
title: "Deploy Jaspr apps with server-side rendering on Appwrite Sites"
date: 2026-10-01
cover: /images/blog/announcing-jaspr-support/cover.avif
tags: sites
---

Appwrite Sites now supports [Jaspr](/docs/products/sites/quick-start/jaspr), the web framework for Dart, with server-side rendering. Set `mode: server` in the `jaspr` section of `pubspec.yaml`, connect the repository, and pick **Jaspr** as the framework. Appwrite builds the project on the Flutter 3.44 runtime with `dart pub get` and `jaspr build`, then runs the compiled Dart server for every request.

Server components can read the site's ephemeral API key from the `x-appwrite-key` header and call Appwrite with the Dart server SDK. The build image ships with the Jaspr CLI, and projects need Jaspr 0.23.0 or later.

